# 42. Role Dashboards: Laboratory (LIS)

Roles (21 + owner): `lab_manager`, `lab_admin`, `lab_receptionist`, `lab_receiving`, `phlebotomist`, `home_collection_staff`, `biochem_tech`, `hematology_tech`, `clinical_pathology_tech`, `microbiology_tech`, `histopathology_tech`, `cytology_tech`, `serology_tech`, `molecular_tech`, `lab_technician`, `pathologist`, `lab_supervisor`, `lab_quality_mgr`, `analyzer_staff`, `lab_inventory_mgr`, `report_coordinator`, `lab_owner`.
**Family rule (LIS):** accession-first (barcode scan), QC gates release, critical never auto-released, TAT tracked per step. Current LIS specs have **0 tasks** per role: add task lists. Common features for every lab role: accession/barcode sample tracking, reference ranges by age/sex + auto H/L flags, critical call-back log, delta check, sample reject/recollect, TAT tracking, QC (Levey-Jennings/Westgard).
`lab_admin`, `lab_receiving`, `home_collection_staff`, `lab_technician` follow the nearest entries below (manager / receptionist / phlebotomist / section tech).

### Lab Manager / Lab Admin (`lab_manager`)
- **Purpose:** Whole-lab throughput, TAT, QC, cost, staffing.
- **Current status:** spec `lisDashboardSpec` · route `/lab/dashboard/lab_manager` · current depth: 8 KPIs / 0 tasks / 3 alerts / 6 queues / 8 actions / 4 modules
- **KPI cards (target):** Samples received/processed today; TAT by priority (STAT <60 min %); Pending/backlog by section; QC failures open; Critical results unacked; Revenue & cost per test; Outsourced pending; Analyzer uptime
- **Worklists / queues:** Section workload board; TAT breach list; QC failures needing action; Outsource tracker; Staff roster vs workload
- **Alerts:** STAT TAT breach; QC Westgard violation; Critical unacked; Reagent low/expiry; Analyzer down
- **Quick actions:** Reassign workload, Review QC, Approve outsource, Order reagents
- **Sections / tabs:** Overview · Sections · TAT · QC · Outsource · Cost · Staff
- **Features:** TAT dashboard (median/90th pct by test/section); QC overview across analyzers; Cost-per-test & reagent consumption; Sample rejection analytics; NABL document control
- **Data / APIs:** `/lab/{tat,qc,outsource}`, LIS spec modules, `/stores`
- **Permissions & privacy:** Lab-wide results, patient IDs visible (clinical role).

